course: dictionary
lesson: 1875
title: Collapse: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To know which one fits, read the words around it, because the context gives you clues. The word collapse is a good example.
explain: «Never go into old mines, caves or tunnels; they can collapse.» Here collapse means to fall down or fall in suddenly. Try it: a tunnel can fall in, so the meaning fits.
explain: «He collapses in a heap in the road.» A person can collapse too, falling down all at once. A plan can collapse as well, which means it fails suddenly. Ask yourself: does the meaning make sense in the sentence?
fact: Collapse means to fall down or fall in suddenly, like a building, bridge or tent.
fact: A person can collapse because of illness or tiredness, and then you must call an adult and emergency services (999 in the UK).
fact: To collapse can also mean to fold up into a smaller shape, as in «a collapsible chair».
fact: To collapse can mean to fail suddenly, as in «The plan collapsed».
fact: Collapse can also be a noun: a collapse is a sudden fall or failure.
exercise: «Never go into old mines, caves or tunnels; they can collapse.» What does collapse mean here? | Become very happy | *Fall down or fall in suddenly | Shout loudly | Shrink in the wash
exercise: «He collapses in a heap in the road.» What does collapses mean? | Jumps up quickly | Sits down slowly to rest | *Falls down all at once | Sings loudly
exercise: Which phrase describes a chair that folds up into a smaller shape? | A bouncy chair | *A collapsible chair | A painted chair | A wooden chair
test: Sam reads «The plan collapsed.» What does it mean? | It was printed twice | It was very long | It was painted green | *It failed suddenly
test: In first aid, what should you do first if someone collapses? | Take a photo of them | Walk away and leave them alone | Ask them to stand up | *Call an adult and emergency services
exam: Which word could replace collapse in «The old bridge began to collapse»? | Sing | Grow | Shine | *Fall down
